LEFT JOIN OR LEFT OUTER JOIN:
-------------------------------

A left join combines rows from two or more tables based on a related column between them. The left join returns all rows from the left table and the matching rows from the right table.

If there is no matching row in the right table, the result will include null values for the columns from the right table.


mysql> select * from student_table as t1
    -> left join ncc_nss_table as t2
    -> on t1.id = t2.id;
