FULL OUTER JOIN  (MYSQL NOT SUPPORTING FULL OUTER JOIN)
----------------------

A full outer join that combines rows from two or more tables based on a related column between them. 

It returns all rows from both tables, including matched and unmatched rows. 
This means that all rows from the left table and all rows from the right table are included in the result set, with null values for the columns from the other table where there is no match.


