STORED PROCEDURE
-----------------------------
we can store set of sql statements in a procedure, we can call whenever we need , stored procedures are used for resuability

A stored procedure is a precompiled set of SQL statements that perform a specific task and are stored in a database for reuse.
It can accept input parameters, return output parameters, and modify variables. 
Stored procedures offer benefits such as reusability, improved security, reduced network traffic, and better performance


DELIMITER //

CREATE PROCEDURE first_procedure()
BEGIN
    SELECT id, age 
    FROM student_table
    WHERE id > 5 AND age > 17;
END //

DELIMITER ;

mysql> call first_procedure();
+----+------+
| id | age  |
+----+------+
|  6 |   18 |
|  8 |   18 |
|  9 |   18 |
+----+------+
